    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #335\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-128-mcp-integration-07-07-invoke-granted-m-thr_bbyz9ukwv7`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements the outbound MCP-invoke adapter for issue #128:\n\n- `resolveGrantedMcpTool` (`packages/data`) re-derives grant/registration/server state for a `(projectItemId, mcpToolRegistrationId)` pair at invoke time, from server-derived run context only.\n- `resolveMcpInvocation` / `executeMcpInvocation` / `createMcpInvokeTool` (`packages/agent-runtime`) validate call arguments against the tool's synchronized JSON Schema, open a connection through the #231 connection factory, invoke over the configured stdio/SSE/HTTP transport, map the result to an `AgentTool`-shaped `{error, result}`, and always close the connection afterwards.\n- Unknown, inactive, ungranted, spoofed, or schema-invalid calls are rejected before any transport is touched.\n- Resolution is split from execution so a future approval-queue composition root can gate on `target.requiresApproval` / `target.riskClass` without this adapter implementing any waiting itself.\n- The shared stdio/sse/http MCP contract test servers were extended with an identical `tools/call` handler so all three transports are exercised by the same test matrix.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm run test` (unit + integration + e2e) — 613 integration tests plus unit/e2e all pass (one transient deadlock in an unrelated pre-existing test was confirmed as a parallelism flake via isolated + full re-runs)\n- [x] `pnpm -r run build` — all 11 workspace packages compile clean\n- [x] `pnpm run lint` — clean\n- [x] `pnpm run check:boundaries` — no dependency violations\n- [x] `pnpm run format:check` — clean\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
